[node name="Text" type="RichTextLabel" parent="UI/HelpPanel/Box" unique_id=1234390104]
custom_minimum_size = Vector2(800, 580)
layout_mode = 2
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "[font_size=26][b]How to play[/b][/font_size]

[b]Goal:[/b] save enough to buy the island (top bar) and press [b]Buy the Island[/b].

[b]Each day[/b] choose where each boat works (right panel), then press [b]Start Day[/b].
   [b]Harbor[/b]: safe (never sinks), small catch, limited spaces.  [b]Deep[/b] (needs the Deep Sea Dock): big catch on calm days, but storms can sink it; the dock's Hull raises survival (20% up to 60%).  [b]Dock[/b]: parked.
The weather is secret until the boats head out: perfect days pay most, normal days less, storms are dangerous.

[b]Every 7 days[/b] you pay rent [b]and tax[/b]. Tax is taken from the clean money you earned that week (dirty money isn't taxed): the first $1,000 is tax-free, then 16%, 30%, 37% and 45% as you earn more. The top bar shows the next bill and how much is safe to spend; buttons turn orange if a buy leaves you short. If you can't pay, the Silent Partner lends the rest at 5% a day; repay within 7 days or your things are sold.

[b]Buildings:[/b] click any building (or the dock) to build, buy and upgrade. Faint ones aren't built yet. 
[b]Visitors:[/b] after the weekly bills, two people may come with rival offers for something you own (for example stronger hulls OR better nets). Pay for one and the other leaves for good, or say Not now and they come back later.
[b]Weather tools[/b] (optional, never needed to unlock a tier): the [b]Lighthouse[/b] (tier 1) can guide storm-caught deep boats home instead of sinking. The [b]Weather Bureau[/b] (tier 3) forecasts tomorrow, but is only right some of the time.
[b]Tiers:[/b] 1 fishing, pearls, crab, cray, deep sea  ->  2 salvage, treasure, whaling  ->  3 smuggling, hidden moorings, piracy  ->  4 oil. [b]Oil[/b] can be hunted from day 1 (click the Oil Platform plot): pay for surveys until one strikes, wait for the permit, then the platform takes 4 weeks to build. A tier opens when you own every building in the tier below and their upgrades reach a set level (the locked building's menu lists what's missing). Later avenues boost earlier ones (supply chains).
[b]Dirty money[/b] (tier 3) is laundered at 70% but raises [b]suspicion[/b]. The higher it is, the likelier an investigation. An informant tips you off 2 days ahead: get suspicion 25 lower by then and they find nothing. Otherwise: no earnings that day, a fine, and sailing ships seized. To cool off, [b]Hide[/b] your smuggling and pirate ships in the Hidden Moorings (one per berth; hidden ships earn nothing but are safe), or [b]Pay off officials[/b] (button by the suspicion bar; dearer each time).
[b]Crown levy:[/b] every 4 weeks the Crown sets a target: earn at least that much this season (you keep the money). The Crown's appetite grows with you: the target is never less than 60% of what you earned last season, so you have to keep growing. Miss it and you're fined the shortfall and get a strike. 3 strikes and you lose the island. From season 6 each season also has a [b]decree[/b], a twist that lasts the season (status bar).
[b]Crowns:[/b] you choose 1 of 6 Crowns at the start. Each has a good side AND a bad side (status bar). As you get rich a rival Crown (a random one you haven't served) pushes for the island (in place of that season's decree). Stay and that season's levy goes up, or defect once to the rival (new buffs and drawbacks, dearer island, some crews leave).
[b]News:[/b] each week one market goes up or down 50% (status bar).
[b]Champion:[/b] pick one at the start. Each has a good side, a bad side, and upgrades only they bring (marked 'champion only'). Win in certain ways to unlock more champions for later runs.
[b]Advisors:[/b] when you build something, its advisor turns up with two choices. Both have a catch, and your choice lasts the run.
[b]Voyages:[/b] smuggling and pirate ships wait in port (a little money, a small risk). Send them on voyages from the bounty board (in their building's menu) for big money paid when they get back. Long hauls pay more but are caught more often. Ships away can't be seized.
[b]Crown favour:[/b] beat a levy by 50% and the Crown owes you a favour. Spend it (status bar) to clear a strike or cancel a decree.
[b]Wildcat well:[/b] once your oil permit is through, a cheap wildcat well earns a little oil before you can afford the platform.
[b]Saving:[/b] your run saves at the end of every day. Next time you start the game, you can carry on.
"

